   =20
    The new backref format has restriction on type of backref item.  If a=
 tree
    block isn't referenced by its owner tree, full backrefs must be used =
for the
    pointers in it. When a tree block loses its owner tree's reference, b=
ackrefs
    for the pointers in it should be updated to full backrefs. Current
    btrfs_drop_snapshot misses the code that updates backrefs, so it's un=
safe for
    general use.
   =20
    This patch adds backrefs update code to btrfs_drop_snapshot.  It isn'=
t a
    problem in the restricted form btrfs_drop_snapshot is used today, but=
 for
    general snapshot deletion this update is required.
   =20
