   =20
    Fixed a problem affecting reinstatement of passive paths.
   =20
    Before we moved the hardware handler from dm to SCSI, it performed a =
pg_init
    for a path group and didn't maintain any state about each path in har=
dware
    handler code.
   =20
    But in SCSI dh, such state is now maintained, as we want to fail I/O =
early on a
    path if it is not the active path.
   =20
    All the hardware handlers have a state now and set to active or some =
form of
    inactive.  They have prep_fn() which uses this state to fail the I/O =
without
    it ever being sent to the device.
   =20
    So in effect when dm-multipath calls scsi_dh_activate(), activate is
    sent to only one path and the "state" of that path is changed appropr=
iately
    to "active" while other paths in the same path group are never change=
d
