 H_CSR
    unchanged. In the original function which sets H_CSR register, they f=
irst read
    the register, then set some bits, and write the whole 32bits back to =
the
    register. And that the special behavior of H_IS (write-one-to-zero) c=
auses problem.
    This patch fixes the issue in the following ways:
   =20
     - Modify heci_set_csr_register() function so that it doesn't change =
H_IS bit.
     - Add interface heci_csr_clear_his() to clear H_IS bit. This functio=
n is called
       after H_IS checking (dev->host_hw_state & H_IS =3D=3D H_IS).
     - In original heci_csr_disable_interrupts() function, it not only cl=
ears H_IE
       bit, sometimes it also clears H_IS bit. This patch separates the t=
wo parts.
     - Avoid calling write_heci_register() function to set H_CSR register=
 directly,
       and instead using heci_set_csr_register() function
   =20
