commit 2fefd5f6688deaaac96497426677ef1333b5982b
Author: Anders Kaseorg <andersk-DPNOqEs/LNQ@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Tue Mar 24 16:41:55 2009 -0400

    Staging: rt2870: Don't call sprintf() with overlapping input and outp=
ut.
   =20
    The use of sprintf() to append to a buffer, as in
      sprintf(buf, "%sEntry: %d\n", buf, i)
    is not valid according to C99 ("If copying takes place between object=
s
    that overlap, the behavior is undefined.").  It breaks at least in
    userspace under gcc -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE.  Replace this construct with
      sprintf(buf + strlen(buf), "Entry: %d\n", i)
   =20
    This patch was automatically generated using
      perl -0pe 's/(sprintf\s*\(\s*([^,]*))(\s*,\s*")%s((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"\=
s*,)\s*\2\s*,/$1 + strlen($2)$3$4/g'
      perl -0pe 's/(snprintf\s*\(\s*([^,]*))(\s*,[^,]*?)(\s*,\s*")%s((?:[=
^"\\]|\\.)*"\s*,)\s*\2\s*,/$1 + strlen($2)$3 - strlen($2)$4$5/g'
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Anders Kaseorg <andersk-3s7WtUTddSA@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh-l3A5Bk7waGM@public.gmane.org>

