    i2c: New macro to initialize i2c address lists on the fly
   =20
    For video4linux we sometimes need to probe for a single i2c address.
    Normally you would do it like this:
   =20
    static const unsigned short addrs[] =3D {
    	addr, I2C_CLIENT_END
    };
   =20
    client =3D i2c_new_probed_device(adapter, &info, addrs);
   =20
    This is a bit awkward and I came up with this macro:
   =20
    #define V4L2_I2C_ADDRS(addr, addrs...) \
    	((const unsigned short []){ addr, ## addrs, I2C_CLIENT_END })
   =20
    This can construct a list of one or more i2c addresses on the fly. Bu=
t
    this is something that really belongs in i2c.h, renamed to I2C_ADDRS.
   =20
    With this macro we can just do:
   =20
    client =3D i2c_new_probed_device(adapter, &info, I2C_ADDRS(addr));
   =20
    Note that this can also be used to initialize an array:
   =20
    static const unsigned short addrs[] =3D I2C_ADDRS(0x2a, 0x2c);
   =20
    Whether you want to is another matter, but it works. This functionali=
ty is
    also available in the oldest supported gcc (3.2).
   =20
