Author: Steven Rostedt <srostedt-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Jun 17 14:03:44 2009 -0400

    ring-buffer: remove useless compile check for buffer_page size
   =20
    The original version of the ring buffer had a hack to map the
    page struct that held the pages of the buffer to also be the structur=
e
    that the ring buffer would keep the pages in a link list.
   =20
    This overlap of the page struct was very dangerous and that hack was
    removed a while ago.
   =20
    But there was a check to make sure the buffer_page never became bigge=
r
    than the page struct, and would fail the compile if it did. The
    check was only meaningful when we had the hack. Now that we have sepa=
rate
    allocated descriptors for the buffer pages, we can remove this check.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt <rostedt-nx8X9YLhiw1AfugRpC6u6w@public.gmane.org>

