    [IA64] Convert ia64 to use int-ll64.h
   =20
    It is generally agreed that it would be beneficial for u64 to be an
    unsigned long long on all architectures.  ia64 (in common with severa=
l
    other 64-bit architectures) currently uses unsigned long.  Migrating
    piecemeal is too painful; this giant patch fixes all compilation warn=
ings
    and errors that come as a result of switching to use int-ll64.h.
   =20
    Note that userspace will still see __u64 defined as unsigned long.  T=
his
    is important as it affects C++ name mangling.
   =20
    [Updated by Tony Luck to change efi.h:efi_freemem_callback_t to use
     u64 for start/end rather than unsigned long]
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Matthew Wilcox <willy-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
