commit 4c60117811171d867d4f27f17ea07d7419d45dae
Author: Wolfram Strepp <wstrepp-Mmb7MZpHnFY@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 15:34:12 2009 -0700

    rb_tree: make clear distinction between two different cases in rb_era=
se()
   =20
    There are two cases when a node, having 2 childs, is erased:
    'normal case': the successor is not the right-hand-child of the node =
to be erased
    'special case': the successor is the right-hand child of the node to =
be erased
   =20
    Here some ascii-art, with following symbols (referring to the code):
    O: node to be deleted
    N: the successor of O
    P: parent of N
    C: child of N
    L: some other node
   =20
    normal case:
   =20
                   O                         N
                  / \                       / \
                 /   \                     /   \
                L     \                   L     \
               / \     P      ---->      / \     P
                      / \                       / \
                     /                         /
                    N                         C
                     \                       / \
                      \
                       C
                      / \
   =20
    special case:
                  O|P                        N
                  / \                       / \
                 /   \                     /   \
                L     \                   L     \
               / \     N      ---->      /       C
                        \                       / \
                         \
                          C
                         / \
   =20
    Notice that for the special case we don't have to reconnect C to N.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Wolfram Strepp <wstrepp-Mmb7MZpHnFY@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Peter Zijlstra <a.p.zijlstra-/NLkJaSkS4VmR6Xm/wNWPw@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org>

