    remove put_cpu_no_resched()
   =20
    put_cpu_no_resched() is an optimization of put_cpu() which unfortunat=
ely
    can cause high latencies.
   =20
    The nfs iostats code uses put_cpu_no_resched() in a code sequence whe=
re a
    reschedule request caused by an interrupt between the get_cpu() and t=
he
    put_cpu_no_resched() can delay the reschedule for at least HZ.
   =20
    The other users of put_cpu_no_resched() optimize correctly in interru=
pt
    code, but there is no real harm in using the put_cpu() function which=
 is
    an alias for preempt_enable().  The extra check of the preemmpt count=
 is
    not as critical as the potential source of missing a reschedule.
   =20
    Debugged in the preempt-rt tree and verified in mainline.
   =20
    Impact: remove a high latency source
   =20
