    mm: add a gfp-translate script to help understand page allocation fai=
lure reports
   =20
    The page allocation failure messages include a line that looks like
   =20
    page allocation failure. order:1, mode:0x4020
   =20
    The mode is easy to translate but irritating for the lazy and a bit e=
rror
    prone.  This patch adds a very simple helper script gfp-translate for=
 the
    mode: portion of the page allocation failure messages.  An example us=
age
    looks like
   =20
      mel@machina:~/linux-2.6 $ scripts/gfp-translate 0x4020
      Source: /home/mel/linux-2.6
      Parsing: 0x4020
      #define __GFP_HIGH	(0x20)	/* Should access emergency pools? */
      #define __GFP_COMP	(0x4000) /* Add compound page metadata */
   =20
    The script is not a work of art but it has come in handy for me a few
    times so I thought I would share.
   =20
