    page-allocator: use integer fields lookup for gfp_zone and check for =
errors in flags passed to the page allocator
   =20
    This simplifies the code in gfp_zone() and also keeps the ability of =
the
    compiler to use constant folding to get rid of gfp_zone processing.
   =20
    The lookup of the zone is done using a bitfield stored in an integer.=
  So
    the code in gfp_zone is a simple extraction of bits from a constant
    bitfield.  The compiler is generating a load of a constant into a reg=
ister
    and then performs a shift and mask operation to get the zone from a g=
fp_t.
     No cachelines are touched and no branches have to be predicted by th=
e
    compiler.
   =20
    We are doing some macro tricks here to convince the compiler to alway=
s do
    the constant folding if possible.
