Date:   Mon May 4 23:29:17 2009 -0300

    V4L/DVB (11804): xc5000: poll at 5ms interval for register write comm=
and completion
   =20
    Instead of polling at 100ms intervals for register writes, poll at 5m=
s
    intervals.  This is consistent with the xc5000 specification, and imp=
roves
    tuning time by up to 500 ms on devices that such as the au0828 which =
do not
    properly implement i2c clock stretching (since the five register writ=
es that
    occur for a tuning request often do not complete immediately but do c=
omplete
    far before 100ms has gone by).
   =20
    The net amount of time we wait before timing out is unchanged (500ms).
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Devin Heitmueller <dheitmueller-eb9eJ82Ua7k9XoPSrs7Ehg@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>

