    tracing/filters: fix race between filter setting and module unload
   =20
    Module unload is protected by event_mutex, while setting filter is
    protected by filter_mutex. This leads to the race:
   =20
    echo 'bar =3D=3D 0 || bar =3D=3D 10' \    |
    		> sample/filter   |
                                      |  insmod sample.ko
      add_pred("bar =3D=3D 0")            |
        -> n_preds =3D=3D 1               |
      add_pred("bar =3D=3D 100")          |
        -> n_preds =3D=3D 2               |
                                      |  rmmod sample.ko
                                      |  insmod sample.ko
      add_pred("&&")                  |
        -> n_preds =3D=3D 1 (should be 3) |
   =20
    Now event->filter->preds is corrupted. An then when filter_match_pred=
s()
    is called, the WARN_ON() in it will be triggered.
   =20
    To avoid the race, we remove filter_mutex, and replace it with event_=
mutex.
   =20
    [ Impact: prevent corruption of filters by module removing and loadin=
g ]
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Li Zefan <lizf-BthXqXjhjHXQFUHtdCDX3A@public.gmane.org>
