    atmel_serial: fix hang in set_termios when crtscts is enabled
   =20
    After enabling hardware flow control, any subsequent termios call may=
 hang
    waiting for the transmitter to drain.  This appears to be caused by a
    busy-loop in set_termios() waiting for the transmitter to become empt=
y,
    which may take a very long time (or hang indefinitely) if the device =
at
    the other end is blocking us.
   =20
    A quick look through the tty and serial_core code indicates that any
    necessary flushing (which is optional) has already been done at this
    point, so there's no need for the driver to flush the transmitter on =
its
    own.
   =20
    Fix it by removing the busy-loop altogether.
   =20
    Tested-by: Eirik Aanonsen <eaa-vv5co6j4La2Rq8AjE7tl8g@public.gmane.org>
