    USB: xhci: Respect critical sections.
   =20
    Narrow down time spent holding the xHCI spinlock so that it's only us=
ed to
    protect the xHCI rings, not as mutual exclusion.  Stop allocating mem=
ory
    while holding the spinlock and calling xhci_alloc_virt_device() and
    xhci_endpoint_init().
   =20
    The USB core should have locking in it to prevent device state to be
    manipulated by more than one kernel thread.  E.g. you can't free a de=
vice
    while you're in the middle of setting a new configuration.  So removi=
ng
    the locks from the sections where xhci_alloc_dev() and
    xhci_reset_bandwidth() touch xHCI's representation of the device shou=
ld be
    OK.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Sarah Sharp <sarah.a.sharp-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
