    ramfs: ignore unknown mount options
   =20
    On systems where CONFIG_SHMEM is disabled, mounting tmpfs filesystems=
 can
    fail when tmpfs options are used.  This is because tmpfs creates a sm=
all
    wrapper around ramfs which rejects unknown options, and ramfs itself =
only
    supports a tiny subset of what tmpfs supports.  This makes it pretty =
hard
    to use the same userspace systems across different configuration syst=
ems.
    As such, ramfs should ignore the tmpfs options when tmpfs is merely a
    wrapper around ramfs.
   =20
    This used to work before commit c3b1b1cbf0 as previously, ramfs would
    ignore all options.  But now, we get:
    ramfs: bad mount option: size=3D10M
    mount: mounting mdev on /dev failed: Invalid argument
   =20
    Another option might be to restore the previous behavior, where ramfs
    simply ignored all unknown mount options ... which is what Hugh prefe=
