Author: Aaro Koskinen <aaro.koskinen-xNZwKgViW5gAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed May 27 17:54:45 2009 +0300

    i2c: OMAP2/3: Fix scll/sclh calculations
   =20
    Fix scll/sclh calculations for HS and fast modes. Currently the drive=
r
    uses equal (roughly) low/high times which will result in too short
    low time.
   =20
    OMAP3430 TRM gives the following equations:
   =20
    	F/S: tLow  =3D (scll + 7) * internal_clk
    	     tHigh =3D (sclh + 5) * internal_clk
    	HS:  tLow  =3D (scll + 7) * fclk
    	     tHigh =3D (sclh + 5) * fclk
   =20
    Furthermore, the I2C specification sets the following minimum values
    for HS tLow/tHigh for capacitive bus loads 100 pF (maximum speed 3400=
)
    and 400 pF (maximum speed 1700):
   =20
    	speed	tLow		tHigh
    	3400	160 ns		60 ns
    	1700	320 ns		120 ns
   =20
    and for F/S:
   =20
    	speed	tLow		tHigh
    	400	1300 ns		600 ns
    	100	4700 ns		4000 ns
   =20
    By using duty cycles 33/66 (HS, F) and 50/50 (S) we stay above these
    minimum values.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Aaro Koskinen <aaro.koskinen-xNZwKgViW5gAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
    Acked-by: Tony Lindgren <tony-4v6yS6AI5VpBDgjK7y7TUQ@public.gmane.org>
