Author: Andrew Patterson <andrew.patterson-VXdhtT5mjnY@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Apr 22 16:52:09 2009 -0600

    PCI: Add support for turning PCIe ECRC on or off
   =20
    Adds support for PCI Express transaction layer end-to-end CRC checkin=
g
    (ECRC).  This patch will enable/disable ECRC checking by setting/clea=
ring
    the ECRC Check Enable and/or ECRC Generation Enable bits for devices =
that
    support ECRC.
   =20
    The ECRC setting is controlled by the "pci=3Decrc=3D<policy>" command=
-line
    option. If this option is not set or is set to 'bios", the enable and
    generation bits are left in whatever state that firmware/BIOS set the=
m to.
    The "off" setting turns them off, and the "on" option turns them on (=
if the
    device supports it).
   =20
    Turning ECRC on or off can be a data integrity versus performance
    tradeoff.  In theory, turning it on will catch more data errors, turn=
ing
    it off means possibly better performance since CRC does not need to b=
e
    calculated by the PCIe hardware and packet sizes are reduced.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Andrew Patterson <andrew.patterson-VXdhtT5mjnY@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Jesse Barnes <jbarnes-Y1mF5jBUw70BENJcbMCuUQ@public.gmane.org>

