    different directions.  One may try to remove the mark because of an
    explicit request and one might try to remove it because the inode was
    deleted.  It's possible that the removal because of inode deletion wi=
ll
    remove the mark from the inode's list, but the removal by explicit re=
quest
    will actually set entry->inode =3D=3D NULL; and call the iput.  This =
is safe.
   =20
