Date:   Thu Jun 11 12:50:12 2009 +0100

    tty: rewrite the ldisc locking
   =20
    There are several pretty much unfixable races in the old ldisc code, =
especially
    with respect to pty behaviour and also to hangup. It's easier to rewr=
ite the
    code than simply try and patch it up.
   =20
    This patch
    - splits the ldisc from the tty (so we will be able to refcount it mo=
re cleanly
      later)
    - introduces a mutex lock for ldisc changing on an active device
    - fixes the complete mess that hangup caused
    - implements hopefully correct setldisc/close/hangup locking
   =20
    There are still some problems around pty pairs that have always been =
there but
    at least it is now possible to understand the code and fix further pr=
oblems.
   =20
    This fixes the following known bugs
    - hang up can leak ldisc references
    - hang up may not call open/close on ldisc in a matched way
    - pty/tty pairs can deadlock during an ldisc change
    - reading the ldisc proc files can cause every ldisc to be loaded
   =20
    and probably a few other of the mysterious ldisc race reports.
   =20
    I'm sure it also adds the odd new one.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Alan Cox <alan-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
