Author: Alan Cox <alan-VuQAYsv1563Yd54FQh9/CA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 12:44:17 2009 +0100

    tty: throttling race fix
   =20
    The tty throttling code can race due to the lock drops. It takes very=
 high
    loads but this has been observed and verified by Rob Duncan.
   =20
    The basic problem is that on an SMP box we can go
   =20
    	CPU #1				CPU #2
    	need to throttle ?
    	suppose we should		buffer space cleared
    					are we throttled
    					yes ? - unthrottle
    	call throttle method
   =20
    This changeet take the termios lock to protect against this. The term=
ios
    lock isn't the initial obvious candidate but many implementations of =
throttle
    methods already need to poke around their own termios structures (and=
 nobody
    really locks them against a racing change of flow control).
   =20
    This does mean that anyone who is setting tty->low_latency =3D 1 and =
then
    calling tty_flip_buffer_push from their unthrottle method is going to=
 end up
    collapsing in a pile of locks. However we've removed all the known bo=
gus
    users of low_latency =3D 1 and such use isn't safe anyway for other r=
easons so
    catching it would be an improvement.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Alan Cox <alan-qBU/x9rampVanCEyBjwyrvXRex20P6io@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org>

