Date:   Tue Jun 2 14:09:47 2009 +0800

    drm: add separate drm debugging levels
   =20
    Now all the DRM debug info will be reported if the boot option of
    "drm.debug=3D1" is added. Sometimes it is inconvenient to get the deb=
ug
    info in KMS mode. We will get too much unrelated info.
   =20
    This will separate several DRM debug levels and the debug level can b=
e used
    to print the different debug info. And the debug level is controlled =
by the
    module parameter of drm.debug
   =20
    In this patch it is divided into four debug levels;
           	drm_core, drm_driver, drm_kms, drm_mode.
   =20
    At the same time we can get the different debug info by changing the =
debug
    level. This can be done by adding the module parameter. Of course it =
can
    be changed through the /sys/module/drm/parameters/debug after the sys=
tem is
    booted.
   =20
    Four debug macro definitions are provided.
    	DRM_DEBUG(fmt, args...)
    	DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER(prefix, fmt, args...)
    	DRM_DEBUG_KMS(prefix, fmt, args...)
    	DRM_DEBUG_MODE(prefix, fmt, args...)
   =20
    When the boot option of "drm.debug=3D4" is added, it will print the d=
ebug info
    using DRM_DEBUG_KMS macro definition.
    When the boot option of "drm.debug=3D6" is added, it will print the d=
ebug info
    using DRM_DEBUG_KMS/DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER.
   =20
    Sometimes we expect to print the value of an array.
    For example: SDVO command,
    In such case the following four DRM debug macro definitions are added=
:
    	DRM_LOG(fmt, args...)
    	DRM_LOG_DRIVER(fmt, args...)
    	DRM_LOG_KMS(fmt, args...)
    	DRM_LOG_MODE(fmt, args...)
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Zhao Yakui <yakui.zhao-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Dave Airlie <airlied-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>

