Author: Hisashi Hifumi <hifumi.hisashi-gVGce1chcLdL9jVzuh4AOg@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Jun 10 15:28:55 2009 -0400

    Btrfs: pin buffers during write_dev_supers
   =20
    write_dev_supers is called in sequence.  First is it called with wait=
 =3D=3D 0,
    which starts IO on all of the super blocks for a given device.  Then =
it is
    called with wait =3D=3D 1 to make sure they all reach the disk.
   =20
    It doesn't currently pin the buffers between the two calls, and it al=
so
    assumes the buffers won't go away between the two calls, leading to
    an oops if the VM manages to free the buffers in the middle of the sy=
nc.
   =20
    This fixes that assumption and updates the code to return an error if=
 things
    are not up to date when the wait =3D=3D 1 run is done.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Hisashi Hifumi <hifumi.hisashi-gVGce1chcLdL9jVzuh4AOg@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Chris Mason <chris.mason-QHcLZuEGTsvQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>

