Author: Jan Kara <jack-AlSwsSmVLrQ@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 16:26:26 2009 -0700

    jbd: fix race in buffer processing in commit code
   =20
    In commit code, we scan buffers attached to a transaction.  During th=
is
    scan, we sometimes have to drop j_list_lock and then we recheck wheth=
er
    the journal buffer head didn't get freed by journal_try_to_free_buffe=
rs().
     But checking for buffer_jbd(bh) isn't enough because a new journal h=
ead
    could get attached to our buffer head.  So add a check whether the jo=
urnal
    head remained the same and whether it's still at the same transaction=
 and
    list.
   =20
    This is a nasty bug and can cause problems like memory corruption (us=
e after
    free) or trigger various assertions in JBD code (observed).
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Jan Kara <jack-AlSwsSmVLrQ@public.gmane.org>
    Cc: <stable-DgEjT+Ai2ygdnm+yROfE0A@public.gmane.org>
    Cc: <linux-ext4-u79uwXL29TY76Z2rM5mHXA@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org>
