    Acked-by: Marcel Holtmann <marcel-kz+m5ild9QBg9hUCZPvPmw@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: John W. Linville <linville-2XuSBdqkA4R54TAoqtyWWQ@public.gmane.org>

commit 19d337dff95cbf76edd3ad95c0cee2732c3e1ec5
Author: Johannes Berg <johannes-cdvu00un1VgdHxzADdlk8Q@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Tue Jun 2 13:01:37 2009 +0200

    rfkill: rewrite
   =20
    This patch completely rewrites the rfkill core to address
    the following deficiencies:
   =20
     * all rfkill drivers need to implement polling where necessary
       rather than having one central implementation
   =20
     * updating the rfkill state cannot be done from arbitrary
       contexts, forcing drivers to use schedule_work and requiring
       lots of code
   =20
     * rfkill drivers need to keep track of soft/hard blocked
       internally -- the core should do this
   =20
     * the rfkill API has many unexpected quirks, for example being
       asymmetric wrt. alloc/free and register/unregister
   =20
     * rfkill can call back into a driver from within a function the
       driver called -- this is prone to deadlocks and generally
       should be avoided
   =20
     * rfkill-input pointlessly is a separate module
   =20
     * drivers need to #ifdef rfkill functions (unless they want to
       depend on or select RFKILL) -- rfkill should provide inlines
       that do nothing if it isn't compiled in
   =20
     * the rfkill structure is not opaque -- drivers need to initialise
       it correctly (lots of sanity checking code required) -- instead
       force drivers to pass the right variables to rfkill_alloc()
   =20
     * the documentation is hard to read because it always assumes the
       reader is completely clueless and contains way TOO MANY CAPS
   =20
     * the rfkill code needlessly uses a lot of locks and atomic
       operations in locked sections
   =20
     * fix LED trigger to actually change the LED when the radio state
       changes -- this wasn't done before
   =20
    Tested-by: Alan Jenkins <alan-jenkins-cCz0Lq7MMjm9FHfhHBbuYA@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Henrique de Moraes Holschuh <hmh-N3TV7GIv+o9fyO9Q7EP/yw@public.gmane.org> [thinkpad=
]
