Author: Steven Rostedt <srostedt-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Wed Jun 3 09:30:10 2009 -0400

    ring-buffer: discard timestamps that are at the start of the buffer
   =20
    Every buffer page in the ring buffer includes its own time stamp.
    When an event is recorded to the ring buffer with a delta time greate=
r
    than what can be held in the event header, a time stamp event is crea=
ted.
   =20
    If the the create timestamp falls over to the next buffer page, it is
    redundant because the buffer page holds a full time stamp. This patch
    will try to discard the time stamp when it falls to the start of the
    next page.
   =20
    This change also fixes a issues with disarding events. If most events=
 are
    discarded, timestamps will start to creep into the ring buffer. If we
    do not discard the timestamps then they can fill up the ring buffer o=
ver
    time and waste space.
   =20
    This change will keep time stamps from filling up over another page. =
If
    something is recorded in the buffer page, and the rest is filtered, t=
hen
    the time stamps can only fill up to the end of the page.
   =20
    [ Impact: prevent time stamps from filling ring buffer ]
   =20
    Reported-by: Tim Bird <tim.bird-mEdOJwZ7QcZBDgjK7y7TUQ@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt <rostedt-nx8X9YLhiw1AfugRpC6u6w@public.gmane.org>

