Author: Li Zefan <lizf-BthXqXjhjHXQFUHtdCDX3A@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Mon Jun 1 15:35:46 2009 +0800

    tracing/events: introduce __dynamic_array()
   =20
    __string() is limited:
   =20
      - it's a char array, but we may want to define array with other typ=
es
      - a source string should be available, but we may just know the str=
ing size
   =20
    We introduce __dynamic_array() to break those limitations, and __stri=
ng()
    becomes a wrapper of it. As a side effect, now __get_str() can be use=
d
    in TP_fast_assign but not only TP_print.
   =20
    Take XFS for example, we have the string length in the dirent, but th=
e
    string itself is not NULL-terminated, so __dynamic_array() can be use=
d:
   =20
    TRACE_EVENT(xfs_dir2,
    	TP_PROTO(struct xfs_da_args *args),
    	TP_ARGS(args),
   =20
    	TP_STRUCT__entry(
    		__field(int, namelen)
    		__dynamic_array(char, name, args->namelen + 1)
    		...
    	),
   =20
    	TP_fast_assign(
    		char *name =3D __get_str(name);
   =20
    		if (args->namelen)
    			memcpy(name, args->name, args->namelen);
    		name[args->namelen] =3D '\0';
   =20
    		__entry->namelen =3D args->namelen;
    	),
   =20
    	TP_printk("name %.*s namelen %d",
    		  __entry->namelen ? __get_str(name) : NULL
    		  __entry->namelen)
    );
   =20
    [ Impact: allow defining dynamic size arrays ]
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Li Zefan <lizf-BthXqXjhjHXQFUHtdCDX3A@public.gmane.org>
    LKML-Reference: <4A2384D2.3080403-BthXqXjhjHXQFUHtdCDX3A@public.gmane.org>
