Author: Steven Rostedt <srostedt-H+wXaHxf7aLQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Thu May 28 13:37:24 2009 -0400

    ftrace: add kernel command line function filtering
   =20
    When using ftrace=3Dfunction on the command line to trace functions
    on boot up, one can not filter out functions that are commonly called.
   =20
    This patch adds two new ftrace command line commands.
   =20
      ftrace_notrace=3Dfunction-list
      ftrace_filter=3Dfunction-list
   =20
    Where function-list is a comma separated list of functions to filter.
    The ftrace_notrace will make the functions listed not be included
    in the function tracing, and ftrace_filter will only trace the functi=
ons
    listed.
   =20
    These two act the same as the debugfs/tracing/set_ftrace_notrace and
    debugfs/tracing/set_ftrace_filter respectively.
   =20
    The simple glob expressions that are allowed by the filter files can =
also
    be used by the command line interface.
   =20
    	ftrace_notrace=3Drcu*,*lock,*spin*
   =20
    Will not trace any function that starts with rcu, ends with lock, or =
has
    the word spin in it.
   =20
    Note, if the self tests are enabled, they may interfere with the filt=
ering
    set by the command lines.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt <rostedt-nx8X9YLhiw1AfugRpC6u6w@public.gmane.org>

