    flat: fix data sections alignment
   =20
    The flat loader uses an architecture's flat_stack_align() to align th=
e
    stack but assumes word-alignment is enough for the data sections.
   =20
    However, on the Xtensa S6000 we have registers up to 128bit width
    which can be used from userspace and therefor need userspace stack an=
d
    data-section alignment of at least this size.
   =20
    This patch drops flat_stack_align() and uses the same alignment that
    is required for slab caches, ARCH_SLAB_MINALIGN, or wordsize if it's
    not defined by the architecture.
   =20
    It also fixes m32r which was obviously kaput, aligning an
    uninitialized stack entry instead of the stack pointer.
   =20
    [akpm-de/tnXTf+JLsfHDXvbKv3WD2FQJk+8+b@public.gmane.org: coding-style fixes]
