    (original patch from Catalin Marinas <catalin.marinas-5wv7dgnIgG8@public.gmane.org>)
   =20
    The cmpxchg and cmpxchg64 functions can be implemented using the
    LDREX*/STREX* instructions. Since operand lengths other than 32bit ar=
e
    required, the full implementations are only available if the ARMv6K
    extensions are present (for the LDREXB, LDREXH and LDREXD instruction=
s).
   =20
    For ARMv6, only 32-bits cmpxchg is available.
   =20
    Mathieu :
   =20
    Make cmpxchg_local always available with best implementation for all =
type sizes (1, 2, 4 bytes).
    Make cmpxchg64_local always available.
   =20
    Use "Ir" constraint for "old" operand, like atomic.h atomic_cmpxchg d=
oes.
   =20
    Change since v3 :
    - Add "memory" clobbers (thanks to Nicolas Pitre)
    - removed __asmeq(), only needed for old compilers, very unlikely on =
ARMv6+.
   =20
    Note : ARMv7-M should eventually be ifdefed-out of cmpxchg64. But it'=
s not
    supported by the Linux kernel currently.
   =20
    Put back arm < v6 cmpxchg support.
   =20
