    [CPUFREQ] powernow-k8: determine exact CPU frequency for HW Pstates
   =20
    Slightly modified by trenn-l3A5Bk7waGM@public.gmane.org -> only do this on fam 10h and fam=
 11h.
   =20
    Currently powernow-k8 determines CPU frequency from ACPI PSS objects,=
 but
    according to AMD family 11h BKDG this frequency is just a rounded val=
ue:
   =20
      "CoreFreq (MHz) =3D The CPU COF specified by MSRC001_00[6B:64][CpuF=
id]
      rounded to the nearest 100 Mhz."
   =20
    As a consequnce powernow-k8 reports wrong CPU frequency on some syste=
ms,
    e.g. on Turion X2 Ultra:
   =20
      powernow-k8: Found 1 AMD Turion(tm)X2 Ultra DualCore Mobile ZM-82
                   processors (2 cpu cores) (version 2.20.00)
      powernow-k8:    0 : pstate 0 (2200 MHz)
      powernow-k8:    1 : pstate 1 (1100 MHz)
      powernow-k8:    2 : pstate 2 (600 MHz)
   =20
    But this is wrong as frequency for Pstate2 is 550 MHz. x86info report=
s it
    correctly:
   =20
      #x86info -a |grep Pstate
      ...
      Pstate-0: fid=3De, did=3D0, vid=3D24 (2200MHz)
      Pstate-1: fid=3De, did=3D1, vid=3D30 (1100MHz)
      Pstate-2: fid=3De, did=3D2, vid=3D3c (550MHz) (current)
   =20
    Solution is to determine the frequency directly from Pstate MSRs inst=
ead
    of using rounded values from ACPI table.
   =20
