Author: David Dillow <dave-i1Mk8JYDVaaSihdK6806/g@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Fri May 22 15:29:34 2009 +0000

    r8169: avoid losing MSI interrupts
   =20
    The 8169 chip only generates MSI interrupts when all enabled event
    sources are quiescent and one or more sources transition to active. I=
f
    not all of the active events are acknowledged, or a new event becomes
    active while the existing ones are cleared in the handler, we will no=
t
    see a new interrupt.
   =20
    The current interrupt handler masks off the Rx and Tx events once the
    NAPI handler has been scheduled, which opens a race window in which w=
e
    can get another Rx or Tx event and never ACK'ing it, stopping all
    activity until the link is reset (ifconfig down/up). Fix this by alwa=
ys
    ACK'ing all event sources, and loop in the handler until we have all
    sources quiescent.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: David Dillow <dave-i1Mk8JYDVaaSihdK6806/g@public.gmane.org>
    Tested-by: Michael Buesch <mb-fseUSCV1ubazQB+pC5nmwQ@public.gmane.org>
