commit bcfb7465c03a8c62c89da374677df56f6b894d44
Author: Ira Snyder <iws-lulEs6mt1IksTUYHLfqkUA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Fri May 15 14:27:16 2009 -0700

    fsldma: fix infinite loop on multi-descriptor DMA chain completion
   =20
    When creating a DMA transaction with multiple descriptors, the async_=
tx
    cookie is set to 0 for each descriptor in the chain, excluding the la=
st
    descriptor, whose cookie is set to -EBUSY.
   =20
    When fsl_dma_tx_submit() is run, it only assigns a cookie to the firs=
t
    descriptor. All of the remaining descriptors keep their original valu=
e,
    including the last descriptor, which is set to -EBUSY.
   =20
    After the DMA completes, the driver will update the last completed co=
okie
    to be -EBUSY, which is an error code instead of a valid cookie. This =
causes
    dma_async_is_complete() to always return DMA_IN_PROGRESS.
   =20
    This causes the fsldma driver to never cleanup the queue of link
    descriptors, and the driver will re-run the DMA transaction on the ha=
rdware
    each time it receives the End-of-Chain interrupt. This causes an infi=
nite
    loop.
   =20
    With this patch, fsl_dma_tx_submit() is changed to assign a cookie to=
 every
    descriptor in the chain. The rest of the code then works without prob=
lems.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Ira W. Snyder <iws-lulEs6mt1IksTUYHLfqkUA@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Li Yang <leoli-KZfg59tc24xl57MIdRCFDg@public.gmane.org>

