Author: Reinette Chatre <reinette.chatre-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Fri May 15 16:13:46 2009 -0700

    iwlwifi: do not cancel delayed work inside spin_lock_irqsave
   =20
    Calling cancel_delayed_work() from inside
    spin_lock_irqsave, introduces a potential deadlock.
   =20
    As explained by Johannes Berg <johannes-cdvu00un1VgdHxzADdlk8Q@public.gmane.org>
   =20
    A - lock
    T - timer
   =20
    phase                   CPU 1           CPU 2
    ---------------------------------------------
   =20
    some place that calls
    cancel_timer_sync()
    (which is the | code)
                                            lock-irq(A)
    |                                       "lock-irq"(T)
    |                                       "unlock"(T)
    |                                       wait(T)
                                            unlock(A)
   =20
    timer softirq
                            "lock"(T)
                            run(T)
                            "unlock"(T)
   =20
    irq handler
              lock(A)
              unlock(A)
   =20
    Now all that again, interleaved, leading to deadlock:
   =20
                                            lock-irq(A)
                            "lock"(T)
                             run(T)
    IRQ during or maybe
    before run(T) -->        lock(A)
                                            "lock-irq"(T)
                                            wait(T)
   =20
    We fix this by moving the call to cancel_delayed_work() into workqueu=
e.
    There are cases where the work may not actually be queued or running
    at the time we are trying to cancel it, but cancel_delayed_work() is
    able to deal with this.
   =20
    Also cleanup iwl_set_mode related to this call. This function
    (iwl_set_mode) is only called when bringing interface up and there wi=
ll
    thus not be any scanning done. No need to try to cancel scanning.
   =20
    Fixes http://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D13224, which was a=
lso
    reported at http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-wireless&m=3D124081921903223&=
w=3D2 .
   =20
    Tested-by: Miles Lane <miles.lane-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: Reinette Chatre <reinette.chatre-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
    Acked-by: Zhu Yi <yi.zhu-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
