Date:   Mon May 18 00:34:33 2009 +0000

    net: add tx_packets/tx_bytes/tx_dropped counters in struct netdev_que=
ue
   =20
    offsetof(struct net_device, features)=3D0x44
    offsetof(struct net_device, stats.tx_packets)=3D0x54
    offsetof(struct net_device, stats.tx_bytes)=3D0x5c
    offsetof(struct net_device, stats.tx_dropped)=3D0x6c
   =20
    Network drivers that touch dev->stats.tx_packets/stats.tx_bytes in th=
eir
    tx path can slow down SMP operations, since they dirty a cache line
    that should stay shared (dev->features is needed in rx and tx paths)
   =20
    We could move away stats field in net_device but it wont help that mu=
ch.
    (Two cache lines dirtied in tx path, we can do one only)
   =20
    Better solution is to add tx_packets/tx_bytes/tx_dropped in struct
    netdev_queue because this structure is already touched in tx path and
    counters updates will then be free (no increase in size)
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Eric Dumazet <dada1-fPLkHRcR87vqlBn2x/YWAg@public.gmane.org>
    Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem-fT/PcQaiUtIeIZ0/mPfg9Q@public.gmane.org>

