    TPM: get_event_name stack corruption
   =20
    get_event_name uses sprintf to fill a buffer declared on the stack.  =
It fills
    the buffer 2 bytes at a time.  What the code doesn't take into accoun=
t is that
    sprintf(buf, "%02x", data) actually writes 3 bytes.  2 bytes for the =
data and
    then it nul terminates the string.  Since we declare buf to be 40 cha=
racters
    long and then we write 40 bytes of data into buf sprintf is going to =
write 41
    characters.  The fix is to leave room in buf for the nul terminator.
   =20
