    ntp: adjust SHIFT_PLL to improve NTP convergence
   =20
    The conversion to the ntpv4 reference model
    f19923937321244e7dc334767eb4b67e0e3d5c74 ("ntp: convert to the NTP4
    reference model") in 2.6.19 added nanosecond resolution the adjtimex
    interface, but also changed the "stiffness" of the frequency adjustme=
nts,
    causing NTP convergence time to greatly increase.
   =20
    SHIFT_PLL, which reduces the stiffness of the freq adjustments, was
    designed to be inversely linked to HZ, and the reference value of 4 w=
as
    designed for Unix systems using HZ=3D100.  However Linux's clock stee=
ring
    code mostly independent of HZ.
   =20
    So this patch reduces the SHIFT_PLL value from 4 to 2, which causes N=
TPd
    behavior to match kernels prior to 2.6.19, greatly reducing convergen=
ce
    times, and improving close synchronization through environmental ther=
mal
    changes.
   =20
    The patch also changes some l's to L's in nearby code to avoid misrea=
ding
    50l as 501.
   =20
    [ Impact: tweak NTP algorithm for faster convergence ]
