Author: Darren Hart <dvhltc-r/Jw6+rmf7HQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Mon Apr 20 22:22:22 2009 -0700

    futex: remove FUTEX_REQUEUE_PI (non CMP)
   =20
    The new requeue PI futex op codes were modeled after the existing
    FUTEX_REQUEUE and FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE calls.  I was unaware at the time
    that FUTEX_REQUEUE was only around for compatibility reasons and
    shouldn't be used in new code.  Ulrich Drepper elaborates on this in =
his
    Futexes are Tricky paper: http://people.redhat.com/drepper/futex.pdf.
    The deprecated call doesn't catch changes to the futex corresponding =
to
    the destination futex which can lead to deadlock.
   =20
    Therefor, I feel it best to remove FUTEX_REQUEUE_PI and leave only
    FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE_PI as there are not yet any existing users of the A=
PI.
    This patch does change the OP code value of FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE_PI to 1=
2
    from 13.  Since my test case is the only known user of this API, I fe=
lt
    this was the right thing to do, rather than leave a hole in the
    enumeration.
   =20
    I chose to continue using the _CMP_ modifier in the OP code to make i=
t
    explicit to the user that the test is being done.
   =20
    Builds, boots, and ran several hundred iterations requeue_pi.c.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Darren Hart <dvhltc-r/Jw6+rmf7HQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
    LKML-Reference: <49ED580E.1050502-r/Jw6+rmf7HQT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
