    Intel IOMMU Pass Through Support
   =20
    The patch adds kernel parameter intel_iommu=3Dpt to set up pass throu=
gh
    mode in context mapping entry. This disables DMAR in linux kernel; bu=
t
    KVM still runs on VT-d and interrupt remapping still works.
   =20
    In this mode, kernel uses swiotlb for DMA API functions but other VT-=
d
    functionalities are enabled for KVM. KVM always uses multi level
    translation page table in VT-d. By default, pass though mode is disab=
led
    in kernel.
   =20
    This is useful when people don't want to enable VT-d DMAR in kernel b=
ut
    still want to use KVM and interrupt remapping for reasons like DMAR
    performance concern or debug purpose.
   =20
    Signed-off-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghua.yu-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
