    ASoC: Add power supply widget to DAPM
   =20
    Many modern CODECs have shared resources on chip which must be enable=
d
    for portions of the chip to work but which can be disabled at other t=
imes
    in order to achieve power savings. Examples of such resources include
    power supplies and some internal clocks.
   =20
    Since these widgets are dependencies for the audio path but do not ca=
rry
    audio signals they require slightly different handling to most widget=
s -
    they do not contribute to the audio path and so should not be counted=
 as
    either inputs or outputs during path walks.
